# Sources for searched replies: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# (info and bestmove), fisher-2aj rules 1, 7 and 10, and python-chess 1.11.2
# for the independently checked exact values. Written 2026-11-23.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions. Written 2026-11-22.
> position fen 7k/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go infinite
# Rule 9 sends info before the reply to isready. The move waits for stop.
# Example for the owner to approve. The ticket cites Stockfish as a witness for stalemate.
< info depth 0 score cp 0
> isready
# UCI go infinite and isready. No bestmove precedes readyok.
< readyok
> stop
# UCI stop/bestmove releases the held move for stalemate, 0000.
< bestmove 0000
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
